From cbabebbe0c6f8801601e425b0ed961f25ef78b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arthur <arthur.miller@live.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:16:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Compile single ~F, ~E, ~G and ~$ FORMAT NIL calls
 without a string stream

A FORMAT NIL call whose control string is a single ~F, ~E, ~G or ~$
directive with constant parameters is compiled into a call that builds
the result string directly (FORMAT-FIXED-STRING and friends). The
finite-float code of each directive is written once with
DEFINE-FLOAT-EMITTER, which generates the stream version and a string
version that collects output in a stack buffer; longer output is redone
through the stream version, so both always agree. ~G's choice between
fixed and exponential form is shared in FORMAT-GENERAL-PLAN. Output is
unchanged.
---
